Keep SWGL buffer textures on the normal image path on SPARC.

The tab hover preview renders PageThumbs output into a chrome 2D canvas and
then presents that canvas through WebRender's async image pipeline.  The canvas
pixels are valid: snapshot/readback from the same canvas renders correctly.
The blank preview happens when the shared buffer texture asks WebRender to
promote it into the compositor-surface path.

On Solaris/SPARC, keep CPU buffer textures on the normal WebRender image
sampling path instead of requesting compositor-surface promotion.  This fixes
display of shared 2D canvas buffers without changing browser UI code, while
leaving other TextureHost types alone.

Dependency: apply after SPARC-07-swgl-native-rgb-texture.patch. Keeping buffer
textures on the normal image path depends on the SWGL texture boundary handling
for native-endian RGB data.

--- firefox-153.0/gfx/layers/composite/TextureHost.cpp
+++ firefox-153.0/gfx/layers/composite/TextureHost.cpp
@@ -616,6 +616,16 @@ bool preferCompositorSurface =
       aFlags.contains(PushDisplayItemFlag::PREFER_COMPOSITOR_SURFACE);
   bool useExternalSurface =
       aFlags.contains(PushDisplayItemFlag::SUPPORTS_EXTERNAL_BUFFER_TEXTURES);
+#if defined(XP_SOLARIS) && (defined(__sparc) || defined(__sparc__))
+  // BufferTextureHost wraps CPU memory owned by shared canvas/image buffers.
+  // On big-endian SPARC with SWGL, compositor-surface promotion can cull the
+  // async canvas primitive into a surface that is not populated correctly,
+  // leaving chrome canvas users such as tab-hover previews blank. Keep these
+  // buffers on the regular WebRender image path, where the existing SPARC
+  // format normalization is applied.
+  preferCompositorSurface = false;
+  useExternalSurface = false;
+#endif
   if (!IsYCbCr()) {
     if (aImageKeys.length() != 1) {
       MOZ_ASSERT_UNREACHABLE("unexpected key length");
